From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:28:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 155/155] GreatDANE: correct the Nov 10 dane.surf pre-masking
 window (round 5e)

Replace the 5d historical sentence. Before the November 10, 2026
logging change, dane.surf's access-log lines recorded the full
request path, including build ID and locale. For about its first
75 minutes online that day they also recorded the full IP address,
and for about 85 minutes the query string and referrer. They sat
in a shared server log that also held unmasked lines from other
hosts. Those logs rotate out within about 14 days. Leave the
pepecoin.surf pre-November-10 statement and the server-error-log
caveat unchanged.
---
 greatdane/macos/PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md   | 2 +-
 greatdane/macos/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy | 9 +++++----
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/greatdane/macos/PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md b/greatdane/macos/PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md
index 89cd82a..b4891fe 100644
--- a/greatdane/macos/PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md
+++ b/greatdane/macos/PRIVACY-MANIFEST.md
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ If a feature only collects after the user turns it on, it's still declared.
   OtherDiagnosticData entry: Linked=false, Tracking=false, purpose AppFunctionality.
   For the Dane update check the purpose is AppFunctionality only; the entry also carries Analytics because of Mozilla's opt-in telemetry.
 
-  The automatic update check sends product, version, build ID, target, locale and channel to Dane's update server (dane.surf). Dane's update checks to dane.surf are written to dane-update.log in the dane_update_masked format: those lines record product, version, platform and channel, plus the request status, the user agent and a masked IP (/24 for IPv4, /48 for IPv6). Build ID and locale are replaced with '-', and query strings and referrers are not logged in those lines. This wording describes those dane.surf update-check log lines; it does not describe the server's default log. Rare server-error logs can contain a full IP. Logs are kept about 14 days, are not linked to an account or device, and are not shared. Before November 10, 2026, update-check log entries on pepecoin.surf kept full client IP addresses; they rotate out around November 25, 2026. Before the November 10, 2026 logging change, dane.surf's own access-log lines already masked the IP address, but update-check lines recorded the full request path, including build ID and locale; they sat in a shared server log that also held unmasked lines from other hosts. Those logs rotate out within about 14 days. No check happens while the DisableAppUpdate policy is on.
+  The automatic update check sends product, version, build ID, target, locale and channel to Dane's update server (dane.surf). Dane's update checks to dane.surf are written to dane-update.log in the dane_update_masked format: those lines record product, version, platform and channel, plus the request status, the user agent and a masked IP (/24 for IPv4, /48 for IPv6). Build ID and locale are replaced with '-', and query strings and referrers are not logged in those lines. This wording describes those dane.surf update-check log lines; it does not describe the server's default log. Rare server-error logs can contain a full IP. Logs are kept about 14 days, are not linked to an account or device, and are not shared. Before November 10, 2026, update-check log entries on pepecoin.surf kept full client IP addresses; they rotate out around November 25, 2026. Before the November 10, 2026 logging change, dane.surf's access-log lines recorded the full request path, including build ID and locale. For about its first 75 minutes online that day, they also recorded the full IP address, and for about 85 minutes the query string and referrer. They sat in a shared server log that also held unmasked lines from other hosts. Those logs rotate out within about 14 days. No check happens while the DisableAppUpdate policy is on.
 
   The update URL is https://dane.surf/update/3/.... This unofficial build does not publish update.xml. https://dane.surf/releases/ 301s to /download/ (as of 2026-11-10). This update-log wording matches the live dane.surf /update/ location (format dane_update_masked; build ID and locale replaced with '-') as of Curb Appeal release 20261111-0308 (November 10, 2026, 9:08 PM CST).
 
